  "releaseNotes": "- `PollAwaitAsync` and `TryPollAwaitAsync`: polling for a condition in async code, holding no thread between evaluations. A synchronous poll in an async specification sleeps a thread-pool thread between evaluations, a thread the code under specification may need to run on.\n- **Requires newer minor versions of other Compze packages:** Compze.Internals.Logging 0.6.0-alpha (was 0.4.1-alpha), Compze.Internals.SystemCE 0.7.0-internal (was 0.4.0-internal), Compze.Threading 0.11.0-alpha (was 0.9.0-alpha), Compze.Threading.Interprocess 0.6.0-alpha (was 0.5.1-alpha). Upgrading to this version upgrades each package listed here too, so their changelogs apply to this upgrade as well.",
